  "id": "Compound::DB00830 - Gene::6531",
  "verbalization": "Phenmetrazine, Diethylpropion, and Lisdexamfetamine all bind to Slc6a2, which in turn binds to Slc6a3. This suggests a potential pathway where these compounds interact with Slc6a2, possibly influencing its function in transporting monoamines across cell membranes. The shared binding to Slc6a2 and the subsequent interaction with Slc6a3 indicate a possible role for Slc6a3 in monoamine transport, possibly as a downstream effector of the binding events. The evidence suggests that Phenmetrazine may indirectly affect Slc6a3 through its interaction with Slc6a2, and similar mechanisms may be shared among the compounds in the dataset. The presence of anorexiant and organonitrogen compound relationships further supports a broader pharmacological context, but the direct link between Phenmetrazine and Slc6a3 remains mediated through Slc6a2.",
